=begin pod

=head1 Highlights

Markdown files are first-class in this release: open one and the editor
highlights it as Markdown, the preview renders it as Markdown, and a
double-click or a drop opens it straight away.

The editor also reads a Podlite document as a tree now instead of line by line.
Every markup code gets its colour, a section name reads apart from a block name
you brought in yourself, and the settings inside a markdown fence are coloured
the same way in a C<.podlite> file and in a C<.md> one.

=head1 What's new

